  "D_Platform"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Condensing boiler gateway",
 "applies_to": "Bosch Buderus SSB800, SSB1000 and SSB1000TL condensing boilers (D_Platform control) connected through a ProtoNode FPC-N38 gateway.",
 "summary": "The SSB boilers reach a BMS through a ProtoNode FPC-N38, which reads the D_Platform boiler control over a serial Modbus RTU link and serves BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP (Metasys N2 and Modbus TCP also selectable). The list has 147 objects: cascade/system values, per-boiler and per-burner status, temperatures, power level, flow, fan speed, burn hours and error data for up to four boilers. Only the reset-curve, warm weather shutdown, night setback, cascade setpoint and boiler address objects are writable.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "50000 + boiler station address (station address 1 gives 50001)",
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The table has no read/write column. Objects whose LonWorks variable is an input/output pair (nvi/nvo) and that map to N2 AO are marked writable; the rest are read-only.",
  "The gateway profile depends on how many boilers the managing D_Platform runs: 63 points for one boiler, 91 for two, 119 for three and 147 for four. This file lists the full four-boiler table.",
  "Blr 1-4 / Burner 1-2 objects only exist for boilers and burners that are present.",
  "The table gives no engineering units; the LonWorks types (temperature, percent, hours, count) hint at the value type.",
  "The same table also maps Metasys N2 and LonWorks (FPC-N39); only the BACnet side is listed here."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "ProtoNode FPC-N38 and ProtoNode FPC-N39 Start-up Guide for Interfacing Bosch Products: Bosch Buderus SSB800, SSB1000, SSB1000TL (Appendix B.1 D_Platform Modbus RTU Mappings to BACnet, Metasys N2 and LonWorks)",
  "doc_number": "Document Revision 4.B (Web Configurator Template Revision 70)",
  "revision_date": "2018-03",
  "url": "https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/service/technical_guides/ssb800-1000-1000tl_bacnet_and_lonworks_start-up_guide_03.2018_us_1.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Set the boiler station address to 1, pick BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP on the ProtoNode S DIP switches, set the MS/TP MAC and baud rate, then select the boiler profile in the ProtoNode web configurator. The list is mostly monitoring: system supply setpoint and temperature, outdoor temperature, power level, per-boiler active/error/service flags and the error number. The writable objects are the cascade setpoint and heating-curve settings; the guide describes no enable or start/stop command.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AV 10",
    "name": "Cascade Ch Mode X SP",
    "why": "Cascade central-heating mode setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 11",
    "name": "System Supply SP",
    "why": "Active system supply setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 12",
    "name": "System Supply Sensor Temp",
    "why": "System supply water temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 13",
    "name": "Outdoor Sensor Temp",
    "why": "Outdoor air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 9",
    "name": "Power Level For Entire System",
    "why": "System power level, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 19",
    "name": "Boiler 1 Is Active / Heating",
    "why": "Boiler 1 firing"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 23",
    "name": "Boiler 1 Has Error",
    "why": "Boiler 1 in error"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 136",
    "name": "Error Number",
    "why": "Active error code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": null,
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Boiler side: Modbus RTU at 9600 baud; set the station address of the device attached to the ProtoNode to 1.",
   "S bank DIP switches S0-S3 select BACnet IP, BACnet MS/TP, Metasys N2, Modbus TCP or single-node BACnet MS/TP (power off when changing them).",
   "BACnet MS/TP: MAC address 1-127 on the A bank DIP switches; baud rate on B0-B3 (9600-76800, factory default 38400).",
   "Device instance = station address + Node_Offset (default 50,000); Node_Offset can be changed in the web configurator.",
   "The ProtoNode web configurator defaults to 192.168.1.24 / 255.255.255.0; change the IP address there for BACnet IP."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Point count follows the selected profile (1-4 boilers); objects for missing boilers or burners will not be present.",
   "Most writable objects are boiler heating-curve settings (reset curve, warm weather shutdown, night setback), not run commands."
  ]
 },
